> What makes our case perhaps somewhat special is a combination of sources of missing data. On the one hand we have (more or less randomly) missing data where sites did not get visited (but do exist); on the other hand, we have sites that actually get created (or destroyed) during the time series. We are modelling amphibians and investigate artificially created new ponds within a set of pre-existing ponds. (I didn't explain that very well, and also omitted the observation model, in an attempt to keep it simple; see below for the full version.)
